# Strict Coding Rules

Mandatory for all code. Violations block commit via `scripts/check-quality.sh`.

## TypeScript / JavaScript

- `strict` mode — no `any`, no `@ts-ignore` without documented reason
- Zod (or equivalent) validates every API boundary
- Functions ≤ 25 lines; files ≤ 300 target / 400 hard max
- Parameters ≤ 3 — options object when more
- Imports at top of file — no inline imports
- Every `catch` logs with context — no silent swallowing
- No `console.*` in production code — use structured logger
- No raw `fetch`/`axios` scattered in UI — use project API client

## Python

- Type hints on public functions; ruff clean
- Pydantic models for API and message shapes
- Modules ≤ 300 lines; no bare `print()` in app code
- Async I/O for network calls

## Security

- Parameterized SQL only — never string interpolation
- Secrets in env — never committed
- Tenant/org scoping on every query where applicable
- Agent tools: least privilege

## Testing

See `testing-standards.mdc` and `definition-of-done.mdc`. Tests are mandatory for behavior changes — not optional follow-up.

## OpenOS integration

When emitting events or exposing MCP: follow OpenOS integration contracts (event schema, audit envelope). See parent `OpenOS/.cursor/rules/openos-integration.mdc`.
